# Electromagnetism 32 — Optics of a Drude metal: reflectivity, the plasma edge, skin depth
#
# (Jackson 3rd ed., §7.5 (eqs. 7.56–7.61) and Problem 7.?; Ashcroft & Mermin ch. 1,
#  Problems 1.2–1.4; Born & Wolf §14.2.)
# The free electrons of aluminium are modelled by the Drude dielectric function
#     ε(ω) = 1 − ω_p² / (ω² + i γ ω),   ħω_p = 15.0 eV,  ħγ = 0.100 eV.
# At normal incidence from vacuum, with the complex index N = √ε (Im N ≥ 0),
#     r = (1 − N) / (1 + N),   R = |r|².
#   (a) ε, N and R at ħω = 1, 10, 14, 15 and 20 eV (the metal is a mirror below
#       ω_p and turns transparent above it).
#   (b) The plasma edge: solve R(ω) = 0.5.
#   (c) The field skin depth δ = c / (ω Im N) at ħω = 1 eV and at 0.010 eV, and the
#       dc conductivity σ₀ = ε₀ ω_p² / γ.
#   (d) The Hagen–Rubens limit at ħω = 0.010 eV (ω ≪ γ): R ≈ 1 − √(8 ε₀ ω / σ₀).

ωp = 15.0 eV / ħ
γ = 0.100 eV / ħ
ε(ω) = 1 - ωp² / (ω² + 1i γ ω)
N(ω) = √(ε(ω))
refl(ω) = |(1 - N(ω)) / (1 + N(ω))|^2

for E in [1 eV, 10 eV, 14 eV, 15 eV, 20 eV]
    ω = E / ħ
    print "(a) hbar w =", E, " eps =", ε(ω) to 8 digits, " N =", N(ω) to 8 digits, " R =", refl(ω) to 10 digits

solve refl(ω_half) = 0.5 for ω_half from 10 eV / ħ to 20 eV / ħ
print "(b) R = 0.5 at hbar w =", ħ ω_half in eV to 10 digits

ω1 = 1 eV / ħ
ω2 = 0.010 eV / ħ
σ0 = ε_0 ωp² / γ
print "(c) skin depth at 1 eV =", c / (ω1 im(N(ω1))) in nm to 8 digits, " at 0.01 eV =", c / (ω2 im(N(ω2))) in nm to 8 digits
print "    sigma_0 =", σ0 to 6 digits
print "(d) R(0.01 eV) =", refl(ω2) to 10 digits, " Hagen-Rubens =", 1 - √(8 ε_0 ω2 / σ0) to 10 digits
